1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,489
Fine. Ahem.

2
00:00:13,072 --> 00:00:14,202
There. Heh.

3
00:00:14,407 --> 00:00:18,707
(Leonard:)I'm no expert, but I think the hook
has to go through the worm.

4
00:00:19,779 --> 00:00:20,799
(Mr. Rostenkowski:)Fine.

5
00:00:21,047 --> 00:00:23,037
(Howard:)Sorry, Mr. Worm.

6
00:00:23,249 --> 00:00:25,739
(Howard:)Sherm. Sherm the worm.

7
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:29,052
(Penny:)Hey, don't name him,
just jab a hook in his face.

8
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:33,720
- You got this, buddy.
- Yeah, come on. Hook that worm.

9
00:00:33,926 --> 00:00:36,056
- You can do it.
- That's great.

10
00:00:36,262 --> 00:00:38,022
(Penny:)Cheerleading. Way to man things up.

11
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:47,727
"...and the control group displayed
significantly fewer genetic abnormalities.

12
00:00:48,274 --> 00:00:51,244
(Sheldon(reading):)But because of flaws
in the experimental design...

13
00:00:51,444 --> 00:00:53,674
(Sheldon(reading):)...relating to environment and diet...

14
00:00:53,913 --> 00:00:58,443
...they lived inconclusively ever after."
The end.

